continent|major-land-region|NOUN|Major land region|One of the very large land regions into which the world's land is conventionally divided.|châu lục|The atlas uses different colours to distinguish the continents.|Cuốn atlas dùng các màu khác nhau để phân biệt các châu lục.|Countable; a continent, continental. The number of continents depends on the geographical convention.|0
eat|consume-food|VERB|Consume food|To take food into the mouth and swallow it.|ăn|We ate fresh bread beside the river before continuing our walk.|Chúng tôi ăn bánh mì tươi bên sông trước khi tiếp tục đi bộ.|Eat, ate, eaten; transitive eat a meal or intransitive eat together.|0
lightly|with-little-force|ADVERB|With little force|Using a small amount of pressure or force.|nhẹ; nhẹ nhàng|She tapped lightly on the window to attract his attention.|Cô ấy gõ nhẹ lên cửa sổ để thu hút sự chú ý của anh ấy.|Modifies an action verb; touch lightly, press lightly. Lightly can also mean without seriousness in other contexts.|-
potentially|as-a-possibility|ADVERB|As a possibility|In a way that could happen or become true, although it is not yet certain.|có khả năng; có thể|The empty workshop is potentially useful as a rehearsal room.|Xưởng trống có thể hữu ích để làm phòng tập.|Often modifies an adjective or a whole claim; potentially valuable. It expresses possibility rather than a guaranteed outcome.|0
unfortunately|regrettable-circumstance|ADVERB|Regrettable circumstance|Used to say that a situation is disappointing or causes a problem.|đáng tiếc là; thật không may|Unfortunately, the last bus left before the concert ended.|Đáng tiếc là chuyến xe buýt cuối đã rời đi trước khi buổi hòa nhạc kết thúc.|Sentence adverb; often followed by a comma at the start of a sentence.|0
